course: dictionary
lesson: 1101
title: One word, two jobs: brake
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Brake can be a noun or a verb. A brake is the part that slows or stops a bike or car. To brake is the action of using it. «The speed a bike loses when it brakes turns into heat in the pads and rim» uses brakes as a verb, an action word.
explain: Look at the words around brake to find its job. «Use both brakes, the front one gently» is about the noun: the parts you squeeze. Phrases like «slam on the brakes» and «put the brakes on» also show how people use the word in real life.
explain: Brake can also mean something that slows or stops something else. «The Moon's pull slowly brakes the Earth.» The Moon is not a bike, but its pull slows the Earth down. To check, swap in slow down: «The Moon's pull slowly slows the Earth» still makes sense, so brake means slow down here.
fact: A brake is the part of a bike or car that slows it down or stops it.
fact: To brake means to use the brakes to slow down or stop.
fact: Brakes use friction, and the energy they take away turns into heat.
fact: On wet or icy roads, stopping takes longer, so you should brake early.
fact: Brake pads are the parts that press against the wheel to slow it down.
exercise: «The speed a bike loses when it brakes turns into heat.» In this sentence, what kind of word is brakes? | A noun: a part of the bike | A place where bikes are kept | An adjective: a word that describes the bike | *A verb: an action, to slow down
exercise: «Use both brakes, the front one gently.» What does brakes mean here? | Bells that warn people | Lights at the back of the bike | *The parts that slow the bike | Pedals that make the bike go faster
exercise: In road safety lessons you learn to brake early on wet or icy roads. Why? | Wet roads make the bike lighter | Early braking keeps the bike warm | *Stopping takes longer on wet or icy roads | Icy roads make brakes stronger
test: «The Moon's pull slowly brakes the Earth.» In this sentence, brake means | Paints or colours | Lights up | Speeds up | *Slows down
test: Which phrase uses brake as a noun, the part of a vehicle? | To brake hard in the rain | Brake and wait for the light | *Check your brake pads before you ride | Braking early on the hill
exam: Mason's team sees the word brakes in a science book about bikes. Which is the best meaning? | *The parts of a bike that slow it down or stop it | The noise a bike makes on a hill | Friction that makes the wheels spin faster | A type of sweet found in shops
